{"name":"Anti-Establishment Mint","hex":"#3f6c45","fetched":"2026-10-24","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"anti","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Opposed to something.","That has a torsion angle between 90° and 180°"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person opposed to a concept or principle.","A fan who objects to a particular creator, franchise, fandom, character, ship, etc., especially on moral or sociopolitical grounds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anti"},{"term":"establishment","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or process of establishing; a ratifying or ordaining; settlement; confirmation.","The state of being established, founded, etc.; fixed state."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/establishment"},{"term":"mint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A building or institution where money (originally, only coins) is produced under government licence.","A vast sum of money;  a large amount of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reproduce (coins), usually en masse, under licence.","To invent; to forge; to fabricate; to fashion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anti-establishment","blocks":[{"text":"An anti-establishment view or belief is one which stands in opposition to the conventional social, political, and economic principles of a society. The term was first used in the modern sense in 1958 by the British magazine New Statesman to refer to its political and social agenda. Antiestablishmentarianism is an expression for such a political philosophy. The growth of anti-establishment movements in the 21st century has been characterised as Neopopulism. Anti-establishment positions vary depending on political orientation. For example, during the protests of 1968, anti-establishment positions generally emerged from left-wing, socialist, and anarchist circles. In the 2010s, however, anti-establishment positions generally emerged from right-wing populist circles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Delete_the_current_government.jpg/330px-Delete_the_current_government.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-establishment","wikidata":"Q1558113"},{"title":"Spring green","blocks":[{"text":"Spring green is a color that was traditionally considered to be on the yellow side of green, but in modern computer systems based on the RGB color model is halfway between cyan and green on the color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D2%AF%D0%BC%D1%96%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_green","wikidata":"Q373787"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Delete_the_current_government.jpg/500px-Delete_the_current_government.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Delete_the_current_government.jpg/1280px-Delete_the_current_government.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Delete_the_current_government.jpg/500px-Delete_the_current_government.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An anti-establishment sign at Lincoln's Inn Fields, London, in 2012","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADelete_the_current_government.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Ken_Westerfield_1977.jpg/500px-Ken_Westerfield_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Ken_Westerfield_1977.jpg/1280px-Ken_Westerfield_1977.jpg